{
  "_description": "Gracenote/TMS station ids for YouTube TV channels, shared by adbtuner_yttv_grabber.sh and apituner_yttv_grabber.sh. YouTube TV guide captures carry no Gracenote ids, so this file is the primary source. Each entry is matched first on yttvStationId (the stationId on each epgRowRenderer in a YouTube TV guide response, which survives channel renames), then on name (the YouTube TV display name) as a fallback. Entries with local=true are market-specific broadcast stations and are only ever matched on yttvStationId, since names like \"ABC 7\" mean different stations in different markets. An entry with an empty stationId deliberately suppresses a match (e.g. a secondary ESPN feed that would otherwise name-match ESPN). Seeded from a New York YouTube TV guide capture (yttv_techpro2004.json), cross-referenced by name against a New York DirecTV ADBTuner export (directv-nyc), a New York YouTube TV ADBTuner export gist by mackid1993 (gist-nyc), the ah4c youtubetv_shield.m3u (ah4c-shield-m3u), an older YouTube TV export (yttv-m3u-json, yttv_m3u_json.json), a DirecTV TVE lineup (directv-tve, test2.json), and Gracenote station lookups through a Channels DVR server (gracenote-lookup), used where YouTube TV renamed a channel but Gracenote kept its station id (e.g. ActionMax HD 59948 is now Cinemax Action). callSign is the Gracenote call sign where the source provided one.",
